<section style="padding:96px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>If you're pricing a new oil tank, you're probably holding an insurance letter or staring at rust streaks and wondering what this is going to cost. Here's the short version: most homeowners in Greater Moncton pay <strong>$3,000 to $5,500</strong> for a new tank installed, plus <strong>$500 to $1,100</strong> to remove the old one. Buried tanks and leak cleanups cost more, and we break all of it down below.</p><p>These are realistic 2026 numbers in Canadian dollars for Westmorland, Albert and Kent counties, not lowball teaser rates. Every job is a bit different, so treat this page as your starting point, then get a <a href="/oil-tank-replacement-moncton/">free written estimate</a> for your exact setup. If your tank is actively leaking, skip the reading and call our <a href="/emergency-oil-tank-service-moncton/">24/7 emergency line</a> at (506) 802-3471.</p></div></div></section>
